# Search the catalog before generating

When the user needs a 3D asset (a prop, an object, a humanoid character, or a
motion clip) and the three.ws MCP server is connected:

1. Call `search_catalog` first with a short noun phrase (`q: "wooden chair"`), and
   `kind: "object"`, `"character"` or `"animation"` when the request makes it clear.
   Ask for `limit: 5`.
2. If a result fits, call `get_catalog_item` (or `get_item_source` for the file and
   paste-ready embed code) and use it. Catalog assets are CC0, ready immediately, and
   cost nothing, so a good match beats a new generation.
3. Generate only when nothing in the catalog fits, or the user asked for something
   custom: `forge_free` for an object, `forge_avatar` for a rigged character,
   `rig_mesh` to rig a GLB they already have.

Tell the user which path you took: "found a CC0 chair in the catalog" or "nothing in
the catalog matched, so I generated one".

Do not paste a catalog or generated asset into the project as a local copy unless the
user asked for a file; reference the GLB URL the tool returned.
